  "description": "T1-Horse Chestnut(Aesculus hippocastrum)-twin stemmed at 2m break-part dead/in distress -remove 2x dead stem sections close to crown break union -reduce remaining crown by 25%(1'5m) to suitable growth points \r\nT2-Holly(Ilex aquifolia) -remove large branch section resting on wall -crown lift remaining section overhanging pavement by 0.6m \r\nT3-Apple(Malus) -reduce crown by 30% to suitable growth points -reduce lateral branch spread to match, shape and balance -crown thin by 15% to allow more light through canopy \r\nT4-Elder(Sambucus) -reduce all stems to previous reduction points -remove any deadwood stems \r\nT5-Large Apple(Malus) -reduce crown by 30% to suitable growth points -reduce lateral branch spread to match, shape and balance -crown thin by 15% to allow more light through canopy \r\nT6-Cherry Plum(Prunus cerasifera) -reduce long vertical branch growth by up to 1.3m to suitable growth points ##[T7 subject to TPO]##",
